   "body": {
    "language": "st",
    "value": "(* ROBOCNC ON AN EMERGENCY STOP AND WHEN IT IS LOST (before the machine logic): every axis is braked\n   and disabled on the stop (robocnc's 81, the reference kept), the drive request drops when robocnc\n   goes away, and HomingDone follows robocnc's homed axes. EmergencyOK is the machine's\n   (EMERGENCY, right after this). *)\n(* homing: RoboCNC per-axis homed bits; required set = X,Y,Z (2#111).\n   Original checked REFPUNKT_ANGEFAHREN_W = 511 (9 axes) with 5 enabled -\n   over-broad; requirement now explicit. *)\n(* AN EMERGENCY STOP DROPS THE DRIVES, NOT THE REFERENCE. The drives go off as the machine's safety\n   chain switches them off, and only a Ready press enables them again (6.1 item 3, 8.1 step 2).\n   robocnc keeps an axis homed across a disable, so a machine that has been referenced once stays\n   referenced: it is homed again only if it never was (after power-up, or a robocnc restart). *)\nF_TRIG_RefEmergency(CLK := EmergencyOK);\nIF F_TRIG_RefEmergency.Q THEN\n\tDriveEnableReq := FALSE;\n\tRefDeclined := FALSE;          (* the reference question comes back after an emergency stop *)\n\t(* ...EVERY time, also on a machine that is still referenced (robocnc keeps the reference\n\t   across the stop): the operator decides whether the axes are homed again (user, 2026-11-11). *)\n\tNcLink.RefAskAfterEmergency := TRUE;\n\t(* EVERY AXIS STOPS, whatever moves it: a program (START_STOP stops it, FAULTS repeats that),\n\t   a move or a jog from the HMI's developer page (sent straight to robocnc), the reference\n\t   run, a pump. robocnc's 81 per axis: braked at its emergency deceleration, then disabled --\n\t   the reference is kept. Sent below until robocnc has it, for all 16 axis slots (an axis\n\t   robocnc does not have ignores it), also when the drives were not enabled. *)\n\tNcLink.StopCode := 81;\n\tFOR i := 0 TO 15 DO NcLink.CmdPending[i] := TRUE; END_FOR;\nEND_IF;\n(* A LOST ROBOCNC DROPS THE ENABLE REQUEST TOO. A restarted robocnc comes up with every axis off\n   and unreferenced; left TRUE here, the PLC went on believing the drives were requested, and a\n   Ready press had nothing consistent to start from. robocnc is gone when its link stays down for\n   1 s (a single failed read is not), or when it answers in RESET (0) -- a restart, or the fault\n   recovery in START_STOP. Taken on the edge: the next Ready hold enables and references as at\n   power-up, also while robocnc is still in its INIT. *)\nTON_LinkLost(IN := NOT CncLinkOk, PT := t#1s);\nR_TRIG_NcLost(CLK := TON_LinkLost.Q OR (CncLinkOk AND MachineStatus = 0));\nIF R_TRIG_NcLost.Q THEN\n\tDriveEnableReq := FALSE;\n\tRefDeclined := FALSE;          (* ...and after a robocnc restart, which lost the reference *)\nEND_IF;\nIF (NcHomedMask AND HomeRequiredMask) = HomeRequiredMask THEN\n\tHomingDone := TRUE;\nELSE\n\tHomingDone := FALSE;\nEND_IF;"
   },
   "documentation": ""
  },
