   "body": {
    "language": "st",
    "value": "(* ROBOCNC -> PLC, first in every scan: the link (robocnc's own bring-up of the drives), the tool,\n   robocnc's state, the head's and the PLC axes' positions, the parameters robocnc writes back,\n   the simulation flag, and the M-codes the running program calls. Machine independent: a new\n   machine copies it as it is. *)\nrcnc_conn();\nrcnc_sync();\n(* restarts itself every 20 days; a wait that spans the restart just ends early *)\nmt_clock(IN := NOT mt_clock.Q, PT := T#20d);\nNcLink.Clock := mt_clock.ET;\nCncLinkOk := rcnc_sync.LINK_OK;\n\n(* drive_connect=manual (cfg/system.json): the fieldbus stays DOWN until a\n   client raises DRIVE_CONNECT_REQ (2057). RoboCNC-native bring-up: raise it\n   once per link-up; a robocnc restart drops the link and re-arms this. *)\nIF CncLinkOk AND NOT conn_req_done THEN\n\twp_conn(ADDR := 2057, VALUE := 1);\n\tIF wp_conn.DONE THEN conn_req_done := TRUE; END_IF;\nEND_IF;\nIF NOT CncLinkOk THEN conn_req_done := FALSE; END_IF;\n\n(* THE TOOL: T1 of robocnc's tool table (robocnc 1.2.0, holding 2250 active, 2252.. T1 X/Y/Z) is\n   the mixing head of the dispensing type, and it is the active tool -- what the original's\n   SINGLEBLOCK('G93 Z=P1710 T1') did. Written whenever robocnc reports another tool, so a new\n   dispensing type, a fresh table and a robocnc restart all get it; robocnc applies it between\n   moves, and the programs no longer carry the G93 line. *)\nIF CncLinkOk AND (rcnc_sync.TOOL_NO <> 1 OR rcnc_sync.TOOL_X <> 0.0 OR rcnc_sync.TOOL_Y <> 0.0\n                  OR rcnc_sync.TOOL_Z <> ToolLenght[A_DispensingType]) THEN\n\twp_tool(ADDR := 2252, VALUE := 0.0);\n\twp_tool(ADDR := 2254, VALUE := 0.0);\n\twp_tool(ADDR := 2256, VALUE := ToolLenght[A_DispensingType]);\n\twp_toolsel(ADDR := 2250, VALUE := 1);\nEND_IF;\nMachineStatus := rcnc_sync.MACHINE_STATUS;\nNcProgramRunning := rcnc_sync.PROG_RUNNING;\nNcProgStoppedB := NOT rcnc_sync.PROG_RUNNING;\nNcAxisMovingW := SEL(rcnc_sync.MOTION_ACTIVE, 0, 1);\nNcTargetReachedW := rcnc_sync.DONE_MASK;\nNcHomedMask := rcnc_sync.HOMED_MASK;\nNcEnabledMask := rcnc_sync.ENABLED_MASK;\nNcFaultMask := rcnc_sync.FAULT_MASK;\nNcHomingActiveW := 0; (* RoboCNC homing is EtherCAT-native; exposed per-axis in\n                         AXES_STATUS only while running - not needed here *)\nNcReady := (MachineStatus >= 2) AND (MachineStatus <= 11) AND CncLinkOk;\nCurrentRow := rcnc_sync.CURRENT_ROW;\nProgramRunningNum := rcnc_sync.PROG_NO;\n\n(* NC actual positions into the P-field mirror (Eckelmann PF convention).\n   AXIS MAP (bench-config! see PORT_LOG): 0=X 1=Y 2=Z 3..6 = dosing pumps /\n   shuttle (vom_nc.mk: C,U,V,W). *)\n(* The TIP position (axis - the NC's active tool), as the Eckelmann reported it: the\n   machine logic compares these with tip heights (IN_POSITION, SHUTTLE_TABLE). *)\nP_VAL[16] := rcnc_sync.TIP_X;     (* X *)\nP_VAL[17] := rcnc_sync.TIP_Y;     (* Y *)\nP_VAL[18] := rcnc_sync.TIP_Z;     (* Z *)\nP_VAL[0]  := rcnc_sync.TIP_X;\nP_VAL[1]  := rcnc_sync.TIP_Y;\nP_VAL[2]  := rcnc_sync.TIP_Z;     (* used by SHUTTLE_TABLE *)\n(* the active tool, for the panel (HMI_POSITIONS) *)\nHmiToolX := rcnc_sync.TOOL_X;\nHmiToolY := rcnc_sync.TOOL_Y;\nHmiToolZ := rcnc_sync.TOOL_Z;\nHmiToolNo := rcnc_sync.TOOL_NO;\n(* PLC-axis actual positions, the original contract: P(16+i) = PLC axis i (P19 B1, P20 A1,\n   P21 B2 / in-line table, P22 A3, P23 A2, P24 side-by-side table). Read through PlcAxisMapped,\n   like the commands: a fixed axis number per pump gave A2 the position of B1's pump on\n   Cubotonic. Relative to the zero the last pump reset (jog 102) took. *)\nFOR i := 3 TO 8 DO\n\tIF PlcAxisMapped[i] >= 0 THEN\n\t\tCASE PlcAxisMapped[i] OF\n\t\t\t0: ax_pos := rcnc_sync.POS_AX0;\n\t\t\t1: ax_pos := rcnc_sync.POS_AX1;\n\t\t\t2: ax_pos := rcnc_sync.POS_AX2;\n\t\t\t3: ax_pos := rcnc_sync.POS_AX3;\n\t\t\t4: ax_pos := rcnc_sync.POS_AX4;\n\t\t\t5: ax_pos := rcnc_sync.POS_AX5;\n\t\t\t6: ax_pos := rcnc_sync.POS_AX6;\n\t\tELSE\n\t\t\tax_pos := 0.0;\n\t\tEND_CASE;\n\t\t(* dosing pumps (3..7) run in full turns on robocnc; the PLC counts pump degrees *)\n\t\tIF i <= 7 THEN ax_pos := ax_pos * 360.0; END_IF;\n\t\tPlcAxisLink[i].Actual := ax_pos;\n\t\tP_VAL[16 + i] := ax_pos - PlcAxisLink[i].Zero;\n\t\t(* ON ARRIVAL, THE TARGET EXACTLY. The Eckelmann NC reported a PLC axis that had finished its\n\t\t   \"go to target\" (jog 110) at the commanded position, and CALIBRATION ends a PMS calibration\n\t\t   on that equality. robocnc's position comes back MEASURED -- a drive following its profile\n\t\t   settles a few degrees either side of the end, the bench's simulated axis too -- through\n\t\t   turns and the pump reset's zero, and never equals the REAL target. So the arrival is\n\t\t   robocnc's own: the move it was given has run -- its done bit dropped after the command and\n\t\t   came back, or, for a move with nowhere to go, has stood for 300 ms (a timer, not a scan count,\n\t\t   so it means the same at any task interval), well past\n\t\t   the moment robocnc takes a request and publishes it -- and from then on the PLC sees the\n\t\t   target, as it did. *)\n\t\tIF PlcAxisJog[i] = 110 AND PlcAxisLink[i].LastCmd = 101 THEN\n\t\t\tIF NOT GETBIT(NcTargetReachedW, PlcAxisMapped[i]) THEN\n\t\t\t\tPlcAxisLink[i].SeenBusy := TRUE;\n\t\t\tELSIF PlcAxisLink[i].SeenBusy OR (NcLink.Clock - PlcAxisLink[i].CmdSince >= T#300ms) OR (NcLink.Clock < PlcAxisLink[i].CmdSince) THEN\n\t\t\t\tPlcAxisLink[i].Arrived := TRUE;\n\t\t\tEND_IF;\n\t\t\tIF PlcAxisLink[i].Arrived THEN P_VAL[16 + i] := PlcAxisLink[i].Target; END_IF;\n\t\tEND_IF;\n\tEND_IF;\nEND_FOR;\n\n(* DIN-handshake P-values (written by the running .din via G21/:P=) *)\nP_VAL[1700] := rcnc_sync.P1700;\nP_VAL[1703] := rcnc_sync.P1703;\nP_VAL[1705] := rcnc_sync.P1705;\n(* Writable parameters come back from robocnc every scan, but a value this PLC wrote is\n   flushed at most 4 per scan in address order: copying robocnc's value over a pending one\n   sent the OLD value back (P2047 kept simulation on after it was switched off). *)\nIF NOT P_DIRTY[1710] THEN P_VAL[1710] := rcnc_sync.P1710; END_IF;\nIF NOT P_DIRTY[1835] THEN P_VAL[1835] := rcnc_sync.P1835; END_IF;\nIF NOT P_DIRTY[1837] THEN P_VAL[1837] := rcnc_sync.P1837; END_IF;\nIF NOT P_DIRTY[2029] THEN P_VAL[2029] := rcnc_sync.P2029; END_IF;\nIF NOT P_DIRTY[2044] THEN P_VAL[2044] := rcnc_sync.P2044; END_IF;\nIF NOT P_DIRTY[2046] THEN P_VAL[2046] := rcnc_sync.P2046; END_IF;\nIF NOT P_DIRTY[2047] THEN P_VAL[2047] := rcnc_sync.P2047; END_IF;\n(* the easy-programming flow rate: robocnc's P1702 is taken only from a running program that set\n   P1703 = 1, and never over a P1702 this PLC has still to send *)\nIF NcProgramRunning AND rcnc_sync.P1703 = 1.0 AND NOT P_DIRTY[1702] THEN\n\tP_VAL[1702] := rcnc_sync.P1702;\nEND_IF;\n(* SIMULATION -- the original plc_keys_fb, dropped with the Eckelmann softkeys and with it the\n   only writer of SimulationActive: the HMI's Start/Stop Simulation is a level, followed here\n   while no program runs (the original refused the change during a run too). P2047 tells the\n   .din cycles; DISPENSING, CALIBRATION and M_CODES skip injectors, pumps and cleaning. *)\nIF NOT NcProgramRunning AND SimulationActive <> SimulationSoftButton THEN\n\tSimulationActive := SimulationSoftButton;\n\tP_VAL[2047] := SEL(SimulationActive, 0.0, 1.0); P_DIRTY[2047] := TRUE;\nEND_IF;\n(* ...and HELD there: robocnc's copy is put back whenever it differs (a restarted robocnc, or\n   anything else that wrote it), and a PLC restart that happens to match the button still gets\n   written. No .init sets P2047: the PLC owns it, and an .init would win over the PLC. *)\nIF CncLinkOk AND conn_req_done AND NOT P_DIRTY[2047]\n   AND rcnc_sync.P2047 <> SEL(SimulationActive, 0.0, 1.0) THEN\n\tP_VAL[2047] := SEL(SimulationActive, 0.0, 1.0); P_DIRTY[2047] := TRUE;\nEND_IF;\n\n(* M-code dispatch: coil scan + ack replaces M_BEARBEITUNG_FB / H_BEARBEITUNG_FB\n   (H-functions: only empty H10 existed - dropped). Bits stay TRUE for the\n   M_CODES / SHUTTLE_TABLE sequencers, exactly like the original CASE. *)\n(* A machine without the pneumatic second Z stage (Cubotonic: its valves and limit\n   switches are not installed) must not hold M450/M500 for switches that never close:\n   there they are acknowledged at once, as the original did. *)\nm_disp(HOLD450 := SecondZStageInstalled, HOLD500 := SecondZStageInstalled);\nIF m_disp.M0 THEN M_M0_bit := TRUE; END_IF;\nIF m_disp.M1 THEN M_M1_bit := TRUE; END_IF;\nIF m_disp.M30 THEN M_M30_bit := TRUE; END_IF;\nIF m_disp.M100 THEN M_M100_bit := TRUE; END_IF;\nIF m_disp.M101 THEN M_M101_bit := TRUE; END_IF;\nIF m_disp.M200 THEN M_M200_bit := TRUE; END_IF;\nIF m_disp.M201 THEN M_M201_bit := TRUE; END_IF;\nIF m_disp.M250 THEN M_M250_bit := TRUE; END_IF;\nIF m_disp.M300 THEN M_M300_bit := TRUE; END_IF;\nIF m_disp.M301 THEN M_M301_bit := TRUE; END_IF;\nIF m_disp.M400 THEN M_M400_bit := TRUE; END_IF;\nIF m_disp.M401 THEN M_M401_bit := TRUE; END_IF;\n(* MAREX: M450 (second Z stage up) is acknowledged and does nothing -- its contahmi.pro has no\n   450 in M_BEARBEITUNG; only M500 moves the stage (down). *)\nIF m_disp.M500 THEN M_M500_bit := TRUE; END_IF;\nIF m_disp.M850 THEN M_M850_bit := TRUE; END_IF;\n(* PORT: one count per dispense. MAINTENANCE counts m_m850_bit_ -- the production counter and the\n   total (manual 7.1), the mixing-head and anti-drip operations (7.10, 9.1) -- but nothing in the\n   original project writes it, so the Eckelmann side must have. robocnc's M850 coil is high for\n   the M-code's few scans and low between parts: one rising edge per M850, as the counters need. *)\nm_m850_bit_ := m_disp.M850;\n(* PORT: a PART pour is an M850 from a production program. The block being executed tells which\n   program it belongs to (rcnc_sync.PROG_NO, the called subprogram's number inside one), so the\n   utility programs' pours -- 8051 cleaning, 8052 manual dispensing, 8053 maintenance, 8054 flow\n   regulation, which every production program calls -- are not parts. Decided when M850 rises and\n   held while it is high, so a program change during the pour cannot add a count. MAINTENANCE's\n   production counter counts this; the total, mixing-head and anti-drip counters count every pour. *)\nr_m850_part(CLK := m_disp.M850);\nIF r_m850_part.Q THEN\n    m850_is_part := NOT (rcnc_sync.PROG_NO >= PROG_CLEANING AND rcnc_sync.PROG_NO <= PROG_FLOW_REGULATION);\nEND_IF;\nm_m850_part_ := m_disp.M850 AND m850_is_part;\nIF m_disp.M851 THEN M_M851_bit := TRUE; END_IF;\nIF m_disp.M950 THEN M_M950_bit := TRUE; END_IF;\nIF m_disp.M999 THEN M_M999_bit := TRUE; END_IF;\n(* second-Z-stage ack on limit switch = the G152 replacement: the .din's\n   M450/M500 block until the stage is physically there (only when\n   SecondZStageInstalled; otherwise m_disp has acknowledged them already) *)\nIF m_disp.M450 AND SecondZStageUpperLimit THEN mr_stage(N := 450); END_IF;\nIF m_disp.M500 AND SecondZStageLowerLimit THEN mr_stage(N := 500); END_IF;\n\nIF m_disp.UNKNOWN_M <> 0 THEN\n\tMessageUnknownMFunction := TRUE; (* original raised NC error 303 *)\nEND_IF;"
   },
   "documentation": ""
  },
