   "body": {
    "language": "st",
    "value": "(* PLC -> ROBOCNC, last in every scan: the drives' enable / disable / stop, the PLC axes' moves\n   (the dosing pumps, in the original's jog codes), and the parameters this PLC wrote (4 per scan;\n   all again when robocnc comes back). Machine independent: a new machine copies it as it is. *)\n(* drive enable edge -> axis commands (10 enable / 99 disable) for the\n   machine axis set *)\nIF DriveEnableReq <> enable_req_last THEN\n\tenable_req_last := DriveEnableReq;\n\tIF DriveEnableReq THEN NcLink.StopCode := 99; END_IF;   (* a later plain disable (Ready) is a 99 *)\n\tFOR i := 0 TO 6 DO\n\t\tIF GETBIT(EnableRequiredMask, i) THEN\n\t\t\tNcLink.CmdPending[i] := TRUE;\n\t\tEND_IF;\n\tEND_FOR;\n\t(* ...and the dosing pumps (PLC axes 3..7), which are not in EnableRequiredMask: robocnc\n\t   runs a motion task only on an enabled axis, so a pump left disabled never turned. *)\n\tFOR i := 3 TO 7 DO\n\t\tIF PlcAxisMapped[i] >= 0 THEN\n\t\t\tNcLink.CmdPending[PlcAxisMapped[i]] := TRUE;\n\t\t\tPlcAxisLink[i].LastCmd := SEL(DriveEnableReq, 99, 10);\n\t\tEND_IF;\n\tEND_FOR;\nEND_IF;\n(* SENT UNTIL ROBOCNC HAS IT. The command used to go out once, on the edge, and a write that\n   failed (the link still coming back after a robocnc restart, robocnc busy in its INIT) was\n   lost: the PLC then waited for drives nobody had asked for, and no homing followed. Each axis'\n   command is written again every scan until the write is answered. *)\nFOR i := 0 TO 15 DO\n\tIF NcLink.CmdPending[i] THEN\n\t\tax_cmd(ID := i, CMD := SEL(enable_req_last, NcLink.StopCode, 10));\n\t\tIF ax_cmd.DONE THEN NcLink.CmdPending[i] := FALSE; END_IF;\n\tEND_IF;\nEND_FOR;\n\n(* PLC-axis motion: dosing pumps / shuttle. Old contract P176+i target,\n   P208+i speed, P240+i acc + JOGKEY. Jog value 110 = \"go to target\" (move\n   abs), +/-1 = continuous run, 0 = stop. Axis map: old idx 8 (side-by-side\n   table) -> axis 6 (W); others identity 0..6. *)\n(* Dosing pumps (idx 3..7): MIXING_DOSING_MOTORS still publishes their speed and\n   acc on the old contract, P_VAL[208+i] / P_VAL[240+i], every scan (speed follows\n   the flow rate). Without this copy every pump run went out at speed 0. The table\n   (idx 8) is seeded from TableMotorSpeed/ACC above. *)\nFOR i := 3 TO 7 DO\n\tPlcAxisSpeed[i] := P_VAL[208 + i];\n\tPlcAxisAcc[i] := P_VAL[240 + i];\nEND_FOR;\n(* The dosing pumps run in PROFILE VELOCITY (CiA 402 mode 3): that is the MACHINE'S\n   configuration now, axes.json \"oper_mode\": 3 on each pump axis (RoboStudio: the axis card's\n   Motion Mode, then Apply). robocnc puts every axis in its configured mode at start-up and at\n   every drive connection, so the program does not request it. A program that needs the other\n   mode while running can still write AXIS_OPER_MODE_REQ (4250 + axis) itself. *)\n\n(* The Eckelmann PLC-axis jog codes: 0 stop; 111 (or +/-n) run at PlcAxisSpeed; 110 go to the\n   target P176+i; 102 PUMP RESET = zero the position counter, NO motion (the port ran every\n   pump after each program end with it). robocnc moves only on an enabled axis and only when\n   the command word CHANGES, so a repeated move word is preceded by a stop. A run is a\n   relative move far away in the run direction, at |speed| -- a negative MT_VEL is replaced\n   by the axis maximum. *)\nFOR i := 0 TO 15 DO\n\tIF PlcAxisJog[i] <> jog_last[i] THEN\n\t\tjog_last[i] := PlcAxisJog[i];\n\t\tPlcAxisLink[i].SeenBusy := FALSE;\n\t\tPlcAxisLink[i].Arrived := FALSE;\n\t\tPlcAxisLink[i].CmdSince := NcLink.Clock;\n\t\tIF PlcAxisMapped[i] >= 0 THEN\n\t\t\tIF PlcAxisJog[i] = 0 THEN\n\t\t\t\tax_cmd(ID := PlcAxisMapped[i], CMD := 80); (* stop *)\n\t\t\t\tPlcAxisLink[i].LastCmd := 80;\n\t\t\t\tNcLink.CmdPending[PlcAxisMapped[i]] := FALSE; (* this word now holds the stop *)\n\t\t\tELSIF PlcAxisJog[i] = 102 THEN\n\t\t\t\tPlcAxisLink[i].Zero := PlcAxisLink[i].Actual;\n\t\t\tELSE\n\t\t\t\t(* UNITS AT THE ROBOCNC BOUNDARY. A dosing pump axis (PLC axes 3..7) is set up in FULL\n\t\t\t\t   TURNS: 1.0 = one revolution, speed in rev/s. The PLC keeps its own units -- pump\n\t\t\t\t   degrees for targets and positions, rev/min for DosingMotorSpeed and its ramp -- so\n\t\t\t\t   they are converted here and nowhere else. Other PLC axes pass through. *)\n\t\t\t\tIF i >= 3 AND i <= 7 THEN\n\t\t\t\t\tu_pos := 1.0; u_vel := 1.0 / 6.0;\n\t\t\t\tELSE\n\t\t\t\t\tu_pos := 1.0; u_vel := 1.0;\n\t\t\t\tEND_IF;\n\t\t\t\tIF PlcAxisJog[i] = 110 THEN\n\t\t\t\t\tPlcAxisLink[i].Target := P_VAL[176 + i];\n\t\t\t\t\twp_mt(ADDR := 3000 + 2 * PlcAxisMapped[i], VALUE := (PlcAxisLink[i].Zero + PlcAxisLink[i].Target) / u_pos);\n\t\t\t\t\tmt_cmd := 101;                                   (* move absolute *)\n\t\t\t\tELSE\n\t\t\t\t\t(* FAR, in the run direction -- far in TIME, not a fixed distance: one day at the\n\t\t\t\t\t   commanded speed. A fixed 1.0E7 was 75 days at 1.5 rev/s once the pumps ran in\n\t\t\t\t\t   turns, robocnc read the profile's duration as an overflow and treated the move as\n\t\t\t\t\t   zero-length, and the pump stopped a second after it started. *)\n\t\t\t\t\trun_dist := ABS(PlcAxisSpeed[i]) / u_vel * 86400.0;\n\t\t\t\t\tIF run_dist < 1.0 THEN run_dist := 1.0; END_IF;\n\t\t\t\t\twp_mt(ADDR := 3000 + 2 * PlcAxisMapped[i],\n\t\t\t\t\t      VALUE := SEL(PlcAxisJog[i] < 0, run_dist, -run_dist));\n\t\t\t\t\tmt_cmd := 100;                                   (* move relative *)\n\t\t\t\tEND_IF;\n\t\t\t\twp_mt(ADDR := 3100 + 2 * PlcAxisMapped[i], VALUE := ABS(PlcAxisSpeed[i]) / u_vel);\n\t\t\t\twp_mt(ADDR := 3200 + 2 * PlcAxisMapped[i], VALUE := PlcAxisAcc[i] / u_vel);\n\t\t\t\tIF PlcAxisLink[i].LastCmd = mt_cmd THEN\n\t\t\t\t\tax_cmd(ID := PlcAxisMapped[i], CMD := 80);\n\t\t\t\tEND_IF;\n\t\t\t\tax_cmd(ID := PlcAxisMapped[i], CMD := mt_cmd);\n\t\t\t\tPlcAxisLink[i].LastCmd := mt_cmd;\n\t\t\t\tNcLink.CmdPending[PlcAxisMapped[i]] := FALSE; (* this word now holds the move *)\n\t\t\tEND_IF;\n\t\tEND_IF;\n\tEND_IF;\nEND_FOR;\n\n(* Every parameter this PLC has written is sent again whenever robocnc's link comes back: a\n   restarted robocnc starts from an empty bank and forgets which parameters are the PLC's,\n   and nothing here would otherwise write them again until they changed. *)\nIF CncLinkOk AND NOT link_was_ok THEN\n\tFOR i := 1024 TO 2047 DO\n\t\tIF p_owned[i] THEN P_DIRTY[i] := TRUE; END_IF;\n\tEND_FOR;\n\t(* the simulation flag always: a fresh robocnc already holding the same value would\n\t   otherwise never receive it, never count it as the PLC's, and let an .init replace it *)\n\tP_VAL[2047] := SEL(SimulationActive, 0.0, 1.0); P_DIRTY[2047] := TRUE;\n\t(* ...and the seed report: a restarted robocnc starts with PARAM_SEED_DONE (2067) at 0 and\n\t   defers every first build until it is told again, which a latched seed_done never did *)\n\tseed_done := FALSE;\nEND_IF;\nlink_was_ok := CncLinkOk;\n\n(* dirty P-parameter flush, max 4 per scan (writable bank P1024..2047) *)\nflushed := 0;\ni := 1024;\nWHILE (i < 2048) AND (flushed < 4) DO\n\tIF P_DIRTY[i] THEN\n\t\twp_flush(ADDR := 4300 + 2 * (i - 1024), VALUE := P_VAL[i]);\n\t\tIF wp_flush.DONE THEN P_DIRTY[i] := FALSE; p_owned[i] := TRUE; END_IF;\n\t\tflushed := flushed + 1;\n\tEND_IF;\n\ti := i + 1;\nEND_WHILE;\n\n(* A pass that walked the whole bank without finding anything dirty means everything this PLC\n   owns has reached robocnc. Latched once: it says \"the seed completed\", not \"nothing is dirty\n   right now\", so a later recipe write does not retract it. Told to robocnc so it can refuse to\n   take a FIRST build of a program whose coordinates we own until we have actually sent them --\n   the guarantee is then enforced on both sides rather than by assuming the operator is slow. *)\nIF (NOT seed_done) AND (flushed = 0) AND (i >= 2048) THEN\n\twp_seed(ADDR := 2067, VALUE := 1);\n\tIF wp_seed.DONE THEN seed_done := TRUE; END_IF;\nEND_IF;"
   },
   "documentation": ""
  },
