      "documentation": "",
      "debug": false
     },
     {
      "name": "HmiRefCancel",
      "class": "external",
      "type": {
       "definition": "base-type",
       "value": "BOOL"
      },
      "location": "",
      "initialValue": null,
      "documentation": "",
      "debug": false
     },
     {
      "name": "homing_sent",
      "class": "local",
      "type": {
       "definition": "base-type",
       "value": "BOOL"
      },
      "location": "",
      "initialValue": "FALSE",
      "documentation": "",
      "debug": false
     },
     {
      "name": "home_pending",
      "class": "local",
      "type": {
       "definition": "base-type",
       "value": "BOOL"
      },
      "location": "",
      "initialValue": "FALSE",
      "documentation": "the operator confirmed: HOME_ALL_REQ until robocnc takes it",
      "debug": false
     },
     {
      "name": "wp_home",
      "class": "local",
      "type": {
       "definition": "user-data-type",
       "value": "WRITE_PARAM_INT"
      },
      "location": "",
      "initialValue": null,
      "documentation": "",
      "debug": false
     }
    ]
   },
   "body": {
    "language": "st",
    "value": "(* SYSTEMREADY AND THE REFERENCE (after DRIVES): SystemReady once robocnc reports the required axes\n   enabled; then, with the machine not referenced (or after an emergency stop), the HMI's question\n   \"Reference the axes?\" (RefPromptActive) -- Yes asks robocnc to home (HOME_ALL_REQ 2068, in its\n   axis order), Cancel leaves it unreferenced until the next emergency stop or a lost robocnc. *)\nSystemReady := ((NcEnabledMask AND EnableRequiredMask) = EnableRequiredMask) AND CncLinkOk;\n\n(* reference run (manual 8.1: READY, then reference): once the required\n   axes report enabled after a READY press, reference the machine\n   (robocnc HOME ALL, EtherCAT-native; replaces REFPUNKT). Sent once per\n   enable; the GUI cannot do this while the PLC holds :5008 (S1.F.2\n   lockout), so it has to be here. *)\n(* ONE REQUEST, robocnc's order. Which axes home and in which order -- Z first, so the head is\n   lifted clear before anything travels sideways, then X and Y -- is robocnc's axis\n   configuration (axes.json home_order, beside the limits), as it was the NC's machine data on\n   the original. The PLC asks once (HOME_ALL_REQ 2068) when the drives are up and the machine\n   has never been referenced; the next Ready press asks again if that run did not finish. *)\n(* ASKED, NOT AUTOMATIC. With the drives enabled after a Ready hold and the machine not referenced,\n   the HMI asks \"Reference the axes?\" (RefPromptActive). Yes homes; Cancel leaves the machine\n   unreferenced -- nothing moves until it is (START_STOP refuses every program start while\n   HomingDone is FALSE) -- and the question is not asked again until an emergency stop has been\n   pressed (or robocnc was lost): release it, Ready to clear, hold Ready to enable, and it comes back. *)\nRefPromptActive := SystemReady AND DriveEnableReq AND (NOT HomingDone OR NcLink.RefAskAfterEmergency)\n                   AND NOT homing_sent AND NOT home_pending AND NOT RefDeclined;\nIF RefPromptActive AND HmiRefConfirm THEN home_pending := TRUE; NcLink.RefAskAfterEmergency := FALSE; END_IF;\nIF RefPromptActive AND HmiRefCancel THEN RefDeclined := TRUE; NcLink.RefAskAfterEmergency := FALSE; END_IF;\nHmiRefConfirm := FALSE;\nHmiRefCancel := FALSE;\nIF home_pending AND SystemReady AND DriveEnableReq THEN\n\twp_home(ADDR := 2068, VALUE := 1);\n\tIF wp_home.DONE THEN homing_sent := TRUE; home_pending := FALSE; END_IF;\nEND_IF;\nIF NOT (SystemReady AND DriveEnableReq) THEN homing_sent := FALSE; home_pending := FALSE; END_IF;"
   },
   "documentation": ""
  },
