   "body": {
    "language": "st",
    "value": "(* ROBOCNC RUNS THE START (START_STOP calls it, after deciding what may start): ProgramStart -- the\n   original's start codes, START_PROGRAM (1) the operator's program, the others the service\n   programs named in their P parameter -- becomes robocnc's build (PROGRAM_NUMBER_REQ, the init\n   version, STATE_REQ build), then run once robocnc reports it built. A start waits for every\n   parameter this PLC wrote and for PARAM_VERIFY, and needs a referenced machine. A fault, a\n   refusal or 240 s without a start drops the request (MessageProgramStartFailed). robocnc's FAULTY\n   and RESET are cleared by the operator's Reset or the next start (RESET, then INIT). *)\n(* -- robocnc state recovery --\n   robocnc comes up in RESET (0) after every start of its own and accepts nothing until\n   STATE_REQ goes INIT (1), so a power cycle left a machine the panel could not start. And\n   FAULTY (13) latches until STATE_REQ goes RESET (0) and then INIT (1). The Eckelmann reset key\n   cleared NC errors from the panel, so the operator's Reset, or simply asking for a start,\n   does the same here. RESET is held until robocnc has left FAULTY before INIT follows: two\n   writes one scan apart can land between two FSM samples and the RESET is never seen.\n   Gated on CncLinkOk because MachineStatus also reads 0 while the :5008 link is down. *)\nIF reset_step = 0 AND NcLink.StartStep = 0 AND CncLinkOk AND MachineStatus = NC_FAULTY AND NOT NcFaultStop\n   AND (ButtonReset OR ProgramStart <> 0) THEN\n\tst_req(REQ := NC_RESET);\n\treset_step := 1;\nELSIF reset_step = 0 AND NcLink.StartStep = 0 AND CncLinkOk AND MachineStatus = NC_RESET THEN\n\tst_req(REQ := NC_INIT);\n\treset_step := 2;\nELSIF reset_step = 1 AND (MachineStatus <> NC_FAULTY OR TON_ResetTimeout.Q) THEN\n\tst_req(REQ := NC_INIT);\n\treset_step := 2;\nELSIF reset_step = 2 AND MachineStatus <> NC_FAULTY AND MachineStatus <> NC_RESET THEN\n\treset_step := 0;\nELSIF reset_step = 2 AND TON_InitTimeout.Q THEN\n\tIF MachineStatus = NC_FAULTY THEN\n\t\tProgramStart := 0;\n\t\tMessageProgramStartFailed := TRUE;\n\tEND_IF;\n\treset_step := 0;                                     (* RESET: INIT again next scan *)\nEND_IF;\nTON_ResetTimeout(IN := (reset_step = 1), PT := t#3s);\nTON_InitTimeout(IN := (reset_step = 2), PT := t#5s);\n\n(* -- start sequencer: build -> ready -> run (level-held requests) -- *)\n(* A start waits until every parameter this PLC wrote has reached robocnc. The writes are\n   flushed at most 4 per scan, the start request goes out at once: robocnc then built and\n   checked the plan against the OLD value (8052 with P1835 = 1 while the button had set 2),\n   and the mismatch latched FAULTY. The original wrote its parameters synchronously. *)\n(* PORT: no start without a reference. The Eckelmann NC refused a program start on an\n   unreferenced machine (its start echo 241 asked for the reference run instead); robocnc keeps\n   its axes homed across an emergency stop, so the PLC refuses here: the request is dropped and\n   MessageHoming (\"Reference the system\") stays up until homing is done (manual 6.1, 8.1). *)\nIF ProgramStart <> 0 AND NcLink.StartStep = 0 AND NOT HomingDone THEN\n\tDROP_START_REQUESTS();\nEND_IF;\nparams_pending := FALSE;\nIF ProgramStart <> 0 AND NcLink.StartStep = 0 THEN\n\tFOR k := 1024 TO 2047 DO\n\t\tIF P_DIRTY[k] THEN params_pending := TRUE; EXIT; END_IF;\n\tEND_FOR;\nEND_IF;\n(* NOT ON PARAMETERS ROBOCNC DOES NOT HAVE (PARAM_VERIFY): a start waits until robocnc holds every\n   parameter this PLC owns, and is dropped -- said, not silent -- when that does not happen in 10 s *)\nIF ProgramStart <> 0 AND NcLink.StartStep = 0 AND ParamsVerifyFailed THEN\n\tDROP_START_REQUESTS();\n\tMessageProgramStartFailed := TRUE;\nEND_IF;\nIF ProgramStart <> 0 AND NcLink.StartStep = 0 AND reset_step = 0 AND MachineStatus <> NC_FAULTY\n   AND NOT NcProgramRunning AND NOT params_pending AND ParamsVerified THEN\n\t(* which program: the operator's, or the one a service request names in its P parameter *)\n\tstart_code := BYTE_TO_INT(ProgramStart);\n\tIF start_code = START_CLEANING THEN prog_no := REAL_TO_INT(P_VAL[P_PROG_CLEANING]);\n\tELSIF start_code = START_MANUAL_DISPENSING THEN prog_no := REAL_TO_INT(P_VAL[P_PROG_MANUAL_DISPENSING]);\n\tELSIF start_code = START_MAINTENANCE THEN prog_no := REAL_TO_INT(P_VAL[P_PROG_MAINTENANCE]);\n\tELSIF start_code = START_LINE_LOADING THEN prog_no := REAL_TO_INT(P_VAL[P_PROG_LINE_LOADING]);\n\tELSIF start_code = START_CALIBRATION THEN prog_no := REAL_TO_INT(P_VAL[P_PROG_CALIBRATION]);\n\tELSE prog_no := NcProgReq;                       (* START_PROGRAM: the operator's *)\n\tEND_IF;\n\tIF prog_no > 0 THEN\n\t\twp_prog(ADDR := REG_PROGRAM_NUMBER_REQ, VALUE := prog_no);\n\t\t(* THE INIT VERSION (PROGRAM_VERSION_REQ 2351): the HMI's choice for its own program, the\n\t\t   default (<n>.init) for the PLC's cleaning, manual and maintenance programs *)\n\t\twp_ver(ADDR := REG_PROGRAM_VERSION_REQ, VALUE := SEL(start_code = START_PROGRAM, 0, NcProgVersionReq));\n\t\tst_req(REQ := NC_GCODE_INIT);                    (* build *)\n\t\tNcLink.StartStep := 1;\n\tELSE\n\t\tProgramStart := 0;                               (* nothing selected *)\n\tEND_IF;\nEND_IF;\nIF NcLink.StartStep = 1 AND MachineStatus = NC_GCODE_READY AND ParamsVerified THEN   (* built, and still verified *)\n\tst_req(REQ := NC_GCODE_ACTIVE);                      (* run *)\n\tNcLink.StartStep := 2;\nEND_IF;\n(* A PROGRAM robocnc REFUSES fails the start the moment it says so: it does not load, or it names a\n   parameter outside P0..P2047 -- robocnc goes FAULTY with the reason and the row. Waiting out the\n   240 s below for a build that already failed left the operator with a Start that did nothing.\n   The next start, or Reset, clears FAULTY (the recovery above). *)\n(* A FAILED START DROPS ITS REQUEST TOO: the service requests (maintenance, calibration, ...) are level\n   bytes that START_STOP turns into ProgramStart every scan, so clearing ProgramStart alone re-armed the\n   failed request, and it ran later -- whenever the machine was next free, e.g. when the operator had\n   asked for something else meanwhile. *)\nIF (NcLink.StartStep = 1 OR NcLink.StartStep = 2) AND MachineStatus = NC_FAULTY THEN\n\tNcLink.StartStep := 0;\n\tDROP_START_REQUESTS();\n\tMessageProgramStartFailed := TRUE;\nEND_IF;\n(* Must outlast robocnc's auto_rebuild_timeout_s (cfg/system.json, 200 s here): a start whose\n   recipe changed rebuilds the plan first, and 8001 takes 83 s to build on the MCM20.1. *)\nTON_StartTimeout(IN := (NcLink.StartStep > 0), PT := t#240s);\nIF TON_StartTimeout.Q THEN\n\tNcLink.StartStep := 0;\n\tDROP_START_REQUESTS();\n\tMessageProgramStartFailed := TRUE;\nEND_IF;\n\n(* the failure is reported until the operator resets or a program starts *)\nIF ButtonReset THEN MessageProgramStartFailed := FALSE; StartRefusedByAlarm := FALSE; END_IF;\nR_TRIG_StartAck(CLK := NcProgramRunning);\nIF R_TRIG_StartAck.Q THEN\n\tMessageProgramStartFailed := FALSE;\n\tStartRefusedByAlarm := FALSE;\n\tNcLink.StartStep := 0;\n\tButtonReset := TRUE;\n\tDROP_START_REQUESTS();\nEND_IF;\n\nF_TRIG_ProgramStopAck(CLK := NcProgramRunning);\nIF F_TRIG_ProgramStopAck.Q THEN\n\tNcProgStopReq := FALSE;\n\tNcLink.StartStep := 0;\nEND_IF;"
   },
   "documentation": ""
  },
