   "body": {
    "language": "st",
    "value": "(* PARAM_VERIFY -- NO PROGRAM STARTS ON PARAMETERS ROBOCNC DOES NOT HAVE (robocnc 1.9.0).\n   A program reads the PLC's parameters (positions, heights, strokes: 8001's dispensing height is\n   worked out from P1818 and P1851) when it is built and run. The PLC used to trust that every write\n   it had made had arrived; a robocnc that restarted unnoticed, or lost a write, ran on zeros -- a\n   dispensing height of 0 is the table. So, while a start is asked for:\n     robocnc says how many different PLC parameters it holds (PLC_PARAM_COUNT 1192) and whether the\n     PLC said it sent them all (PLC_SEED_SEEN 1193); with nothing left to send here, it must hold at\n     least as many as this PLC owns (p_owned) -> ParamsVerified, START_STOP's gate.\n   Fewer for half a second: robocnc lost them -> every owned parameter is sent again and the seed\n   reported again. Not verified 10 s after the start was asked for -> ParamsVerifyFailed: START_STOP\n   drops the start and says so (MessageProgramStartFailed). robocnc refuses a build or a run of its\n   own while a linked PLC has not reported the seed (NC_REFUSED_PLC_PARAMS), so both sides hold. *)\nParamsVerified := FALSE;\nlost := FALSE;\nIF CncLinkOk AND ProgramStart <> 0 THEN\n\trd_count(ADDR := 1192);\n\trd_seed(ADDR := 1193);\n\towned := 0;\n\tdirty := FALSE;\n\tFOR k := 1024 TO 2047 DO\n\t\tIF p_owned[k] THEN owned := owned + 1; END_IF;\n\t\tIF P_DIRTY[k] THEN dirty := TRUE; END_IF;\n\tEND_FOR;\n\tIF rd_count.VALID AND rd_seed.VALID AND NOT dirty THEN\n\t\tlost := seed_done AND rd_count.VALUE < owned;\n\t\tParamsVerified := rd_seed.VALUE = 1 AND rd_count.VALUE >= owned;\n\tEND_IF;\nEND_IF;\nTON_Lost(IN := lost, PT := t#500ms);\nIF TON_Lost.Q THEN\n\tFOR k := 1024 TO 2047 DO\n\t\tIF p_owned[k] THEN P_DIRTY[k] := TRUE; END_IF;\n\tEND_FOR;\n\tseed_done := FALSE;\nEND_IF;\nTON_Wait(IN := CncLinkOk AND ProgramStart <> 0 AND NOT ParamsVerified, PT := t#10s);\nParamsVerifyFailed := TON_Wait.Q;"
   },
   "documentation": ""
  }
 ],
